# Minimal, reuse-first changes

Source of truth: AGENTS.md, section "Minimal, reuse-first changes". Review every diff with the `campus-motion-minimal-change` skill in .agents/skills/ before hand-off.

1. Search before writing: `grep -rn "<word>" lib test`, the widget catalog in docs/DESIGN.md, the services in docs/API.md.
2. Reuse existing code as is; otherwise add an optional parameter or variant to it; create new code only when neither works.
3. One rule, one place. Never copy a block and adjust it; call or extract the original.
4. Touch only what the issue needs: no renames, moves, reformatting of untouched code or unrelated fixes.
5. No unused parameters, methods or imports, no commented-out code, no single-use abstractions, no new package without approval.
6. Efficient by default: fetch once per screen and never in `build()`, use API filters (`limit`, `after`) instead of filtering on the device, `Future.wait` for independent requests, `ListView.builder` for growing lists, `const` constructors, dispose controllers.
7. Aim for at most about 400 changed lines outside tests; split larger work into several issues.
8. The PR description lists what was reused and why each new widget, method, file or package was needed.
